ENTRY            D6491   20260821   20261124   20261124       D153
SUBENT        D6491001   20260821   20261124   20261124       D153
BIB                 11         25
TITLE      Investigation of the mass distribution of the
            28Si+158Gd system: role of shell effects
AUTHOR     (P.Kaur, M.Maiti, R.Kumar, A.Singh, H.Sharma,
            Y.Arafat, N.Saneesh, A.Parihari, M.Kumar, K.S.Golda,
            A.Jhingan, P.Sugathan)
INSTITUTE  (3INDIRR,3INDNSD,3INDDLH)
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,110,034613,2024)
           #doi:10.1103/PhysRevC.110.034613
FACILITY   (VDGT,3INDNSD) 15UD Pelletron Accelerator
SAMPLE     (64-GD-158,ENR=0.97) A gadolinium oxide target of
            thickness ~110 ug/cm2 with a carbon backing of
            thickness ~35 ug/cm2.
INC-SOURCE The target is bombarded by the pulsed beam of 28Si
            ions with a repetition of 250 ns at laboratory energy
            within 120-140 MeV.
DETECTOR   (MWPC) Two identical isobutane-filled detectors
            (20 x 10 cm2, 4 mbar) were placed at +/-70 degree and
            25 cm from the target, with position and timing
            resolutions of ~1.2 mm and 500 ps, respectively.
           (SIBAR) Two detectors placed at +/-12 degree with
            respect to the beam direction to normalized the beam
            flux.
METHOD     (TOF)
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) No information on the source of uncertainty
HISTORY    (20260821C) A.Gandhi
ENDBIB              25
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           28
